# Vercel serves every uploaded file at its own path, so anything committed at the
# repo root was reachable on the live domain: the technical audit (a 51KB list of
# known weaknesses with file:line references), the database schema, and the test
# suites were all readable by anyone who guessed the filename.
#
# None of them contain secrets, but the audit in particular is a map of where to
# push. These stay in git for whoever works on the code and are simply not
# uploaded to the deployment.
#
# Do NOT add package.json here: Vercel reads it to pick the Node version.
# Everything the site actually needs at runtime - api/, assets/, the HTML pages,
# vercel.json, favicon.svg, manifest.webmanifest, robots.txt - must stay.

*.md
scripts/
supabase/

# Design mockups of the admin screens. cleanUrls made them reachable without the
# .html, so /stitch_komb_operational_suite/admin_dashboard_komb/code served a
# full picture of the admin UI to anyone. Nothing at runtime references them.
stitch_komb_operational_suite/
